      {
        "n": "Panorama Yerevan - Armenian Lullabies Special (R)",
        "s": "2026-11-15T01:00:00Z",
        "e": "2026-11-15T02:00:00Z",
        "d": "In this episode Lucia Kagramanyan delves deep into the Armenian lullaby tradition and the authorship of women behind this ancient craft, and transmission of sorrow, trauma and joys of Armenian people reflected in it. Hear lullabies from different parts of Western and Eastern Armenia following folk tradition as well as lullabies in classical pop, opera from the Soviet period.\nThe project is curated by League of Tenders, as a part of Vleeshal's Nomadic Program 2024–2025, entitled “Repetition is a Form of Changing.” Vleeshal is a center for contemporary art in Middelburg, the Netherlands, recognized for versatile, vibrant, and vital projects presented both within the walls of its unique Gothic exhibition space and beyond.",
        "j": "Armenian Lullabies Special",
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/panorama-yerevan/episodes/panorama-yerevan-19th-october-2024",
        "t": "restream"
      },
